.TH "SSOOSSH" "1" "Aug 2026" "ssoossh" ""

.SH NAME
ssoossh-service-retrieve - Retrieve a service certificate using a previously issued enrollment code.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh service retrieve [flags] [args]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Redeems an enrollment code from \fBservice enroll\fR, writing the certificate to <key>-cert.pub and checking local disk to avoid unnecessary server calls.

.PP
The certificate is skipped (exit 0) if one at <key>-cert.pub is valid beyond --grace (default 1 minute) unless --force is passed. If retrieval fails but a still-valid certificate exists, a warning is printed and exit 0 is returned (so \fBMatch exec\fR does not block SSH when the server is temporarily unreachable). Only when there is no readable, valid certificate does an error return a non-zero exit.

.PP
The key files follow OpenSSH naming: the private key is <name>, the public key is <name>\&.pub, and the certificate is <name>-cert.pub.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--code\fP=""
	enrollment code (required)

.PP
\fB--force\fP[=false]
	retrieve a new certificate even if a valid one exists on disk

.PP
\fB--grace\fP="1m"
	how much validity a certificate on disk must still have to be kept, e.g. 30s, 5m, 1h

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for retrieve

.PP
\fB--key\fP=""
	keypair path (relative or absolute; required)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	path to an extra config file, merged after the standard locations

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	server address, e.g. https://ssh.example.com; https is assumed when no scheme is given

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	trace what the command is doing, to stderr; repeat for more (-v steps, -vv requests and files, -vvv bodies)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # From cron or a systemd timer: refresh only when the certificate is about to expire
  ssoossh service retrieve --code "$ENROLLMENT_CODE" --key /var/lib/deploy/.ssh/id_deploy

  # Fetch a new certificate even if the one on disk is still valid
  ssoossh service retrieve --code "$ENROLLMENT_CODE" --key /var/lib/deploy/.ssh/id_deploy --force
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBssoossh-service(1)\fP


